{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_mailbox_sizing", "label": "Mailbox sizing", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "The decision guide for bounding a mailbox: capacity and policy are both deliberate choices, taken where you can say which messages are safe to lose.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_unbounded_default", "label": "Unbounded mailbox as the honest default", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Between v0.10 and v0.15 every mailbox was bounded at 10000 with drop-head, so a Terminated signal, a delivery confirmation and a WebSocket close all rode the same queue and each became a filed defect. The ceiling was not even real, since system messages were never capped.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_backlog_warning", "label": "Backlog warning at 10000 and each doubling", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Always on and needing no metrics stack, so heap exhaustion from an unbounded queue announces itself well before it arrives; the metric series only exists above the same mark.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_depth_is_not_throughput", "label": "Queue depth is not a throughput problem", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Both queues inside a mailbox are ring buffers, so a queue of a million costs the same per message as a queue of ten; what depth costs is memory and latency, and neither is fixed by a faster queue.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_overflow_policies", "label": "The three overflow policies", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "reject when the sender should retry or alert, drop-head when stale data is wrong, drop-new when queued work is precious. There is no best, only what the right answer on overflow is.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_capacity_selection", "label": "Picking a mailbox capacity", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Worst-case burst size, capacity times bytes per message for the memory bound, and capacity over drain rate for the worst-case latency a message waits.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_wait_is_the_earlier_signal", "label": "Wait is the earlier backlog signal", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Depth has a 10000-message floor before it reports anything while wait climbs as soon as an actor stops keeping up; wait has no labels, so pair it with depth for the path once it fires.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_prioritymailbox", "label": "PriorityMailbox with a bound", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "withMailbox and withMailboxCapacity cannot combine, so capacity goes on the mailbox options. drop-head is deliberately absent, since a priority queue head is the message you called most important; drop-lowest-priority sheds from the other end.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_blanket_bounding_pitfall", "label": "Blanket-bounding every actor", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A bound can only be decided where someone knows which messages are expendable; applied across the board it reaches a death-watch subscriber, a delivery producer or a WebSocket hub, which is exactly the shape the unbounded default exists to prevent.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_mailbox_sizing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_unbounded_default", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_mailbox_sizing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_backlog_warning", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/operations/tuning/mailbox-sizing.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_mailbox_sizing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_operations_tuning_mailbox_sizing_depth_is_not_throughput", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/doc